DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ddeevv__rreefftthhrreeaadd() (or ddeevvvvnn__rreefftthhrreeaadd()) and ddeevv__rreelltthhrreeaadd() routines
     provide a safe way to access devfs(5) devices that may be concurrently
     destroyed by ddeessttrrooyy__ddeevv() (e.g., removable media).

     If successful, ddeevv__rreefftthhrreeaadd() and ddeevvvvnn__rreefftthhrreeaadd() acquire a "thread
     reference" to the associated _s_t_r_u_c_t _c_d_e_v and return a non-NULL pointer to
     the cdev's _s_t_r_u_c_t _c_d_e_v_s_w method table.  For the duration of that refer‐
     ence, the cdev's associated private data and method table object are
     valid.  Destruction of the cdev sleeps until the thread reference is re‐
     leased.

     A reference cannot prevent media removal.  It is an implementation detail
     of individual drivers how method calls from callers with ddeevv__rreefftthhrreeaadd()
     references are handled when the device is pending destruction.  A common
     behavior for disk devices is to return the ENXIO status, but that is not
     required by this KPI.

     The ddeevvvvnn__rreefftthhrreeaadd() variant of ddeevv__rreefftthhrreeaadd() extracts the _s_t_r_u_c_t _c_d_e_v
     pointer out of the VCHR vnode(9) automatically before performing the same
     actions as ddeevv__rreefftthhrreeaadd().  Additionally, a pointer to the _s_t_r_u_c_t _c_d_e_v
     is returned to the caller via _*_d_e_v_p.  ddeevvvvnn__rreefftthhrreeaadd() correctly handles
     possible parallel reclamation of the vnode.

     ddeevv__rreelltthhrreeaadd() is used to release a reference to a _s_t_r_u_c_t _c_d_e_v.
     ddeevv__rreelltthhrreeaadd() mmuusstt only be invoked when the associated invocation of
     ddeevv__rreefftthhrreeaadd() or ddeevvvvnn__rreefftthhrreeaadd() returned a non-NULL _s_t_r_u_c_t _c_d_e_v_s_w _*.

